0 -14 Td
(1. Why is ACK needed?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - ACK confirms successful delivery of a specific sequence number, so the) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     sender knows when it can move to the next packet.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(2. Why is timeout needed?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Timeout allows the sender to recover when data or ACK is lost by) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     triggering retransmission after waiting for a bounded period.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(3. Why can duplicate messages occur?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - If ACK is lost, the sender retransmits the same packet. The receiver may) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     already have processed it, so the same sequence number arrives again.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(4. What happens when packet loss increases?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Retransmissions increase, transfer time increases, and protocol overhead) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     increases, reducing effective performance.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(5. How is this method similar to TCP?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - It uses reliability concepts similar to TCP: sequence tracking,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     acknowledgment, timeout, and retransmission.) Tj
ET
